revert the deployed SHA/image or restore the prior ensure-script if the new path wedges or mis-adopts","The reclaim path performs a hard reset and explicitly states 'No recovery ref pins the reclaimed object graph' — the reset itself has no undo"],"finding":"The plan deploys changed runtime behavior (convergence/reclaim logic and a new BOT_PATHS entry) to the running AWS review-bot but does not state an explicit, cheap rollback/back-out path if the deployed convergence or reclaim adoption misbehaves in production.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe27e64ce9716cdcd","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Deployment bootstrap section / operator-attested AC","norm_id":"ne01bd907a121af05","priority":0.066,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":["Deployed convergence misclassifies ancestry and resets the persistent clone incorrectly on the box","A bad ensure-script self-deploys via BOT_PATHS and health checks fail"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a short rollback note to the Deployment bootstrap section: revert the merged change and let autodeploy redeploy the prior SHA/image; document the manual-restore step for the persistent clone if a reclaim reset was applied in error, since no recovery ref exists.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":